{# The worker profile, run by every sub-agent the lead delegates to.

   **No plan-first block, and not by omission.** `_blocks/plan_first.md.j2` renders only
   where the todo writers are bound, and a worker binds none of them, so the block is empty
   here whatever this template does. A worker has one objective and a few tool turns, so a
   plan is overhead.

   **Delegation follows the binding.** A sub-agent at depth 1 binds
   `run_subagent` and gets the delegation paragraph. A sub-agent at depth 2 binds no
   `run_subagent`, so the paragraph does not render and the tool section does not name it. The binding is the limit, because a model can ignore its instructions.

   **The verdict block** renders for a sub-agent whose `purpose` is `review`. The organizer
   reads the fenced JSON block at the end of the report.

   Citing matters more here than in the other two profiles: the handles a worker allocates
   are the lead's handles, because it runs on the lead's chat session, and they are how the
   lead's answer points at what the worker actually read.
#}
